---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { getPost } from '../../data/posts';

const post = getPost('create-a-content');
---

<ArticleLayout
  kind="blog"
  post={post}
  title="How to Add A+ Content to Your Amazon Listing"
  highlight="A+ Content"
  metaTitle={`${post.title} | Share It Studio Blog`}
>
  <div class="article-body">
    <!-- Sección 1: Importancia -->
    <section id="importance">
      <h2>Why Is It Important to Have A+ Content on Your Listing?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Build Customer Trust:</strong> Amazon A+ content is one of the most effective ways to increase
          customer trust, boost your conversion rates, and drive overall product sales.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Drive Conversions:</strong> A+ content persuades potential buyers by providing a clearer, more
          engaging understanding of your product's value proposition.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 2: Contexto y Personalización -->
    <section id="customization">
      <h2>Unlocking the Power of Custom A+ Content</h2>
      <p>
        Since 2019, Amazon has made A+ content available for brand-registered third-party sellers—and this premium
        feature is currently free to create.
      </p>
      <p>
        As we explained in our preview video, Amazon offers pre-built modules so you can customize your listing, provide
        richer descriptions, and keep potential customers engaged.
      </p>

      <p>
        However, relying solely on default modules can lead to blocks of dense text that don't convert well.
        Fortunately, <strong>Amazon A+ Content can be fully customized</strong> with high-quality images, large
        infographics, and strategic descriptive copy.
      </p>

      <aside class="cta-callout">
        <p>
          Want to see how custom designs can transform your listing? Watch our preview video where we showcase the
          high-converting A+ Content we design for our clients!
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 3: Guía Paso a Paso -->
    <section id="step-by-step-guide">
      <h2>A Step-by-Step Guide on How to Add A+ Content to Your Listing</h2>
      <p>
        Now that you know how A+ Content benefits your brand, follow these simple steps to upload your content directly
        in Amazon Seller Central:
      </p>

      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Log in to Amazon Seller Central</h3>
          <p>
            Access your Amazon Seller Central account, navigate to the <strong>Advertising</strong> menu, and click on{' '}
            <strong>A+ Content Manager</strong>.
          </p>
          <figure>
            <!-- Reemplazar con la ruta de tu imagen -->
            <img
              src="path-to-image-seller-central.jpg"
              alt="Navigating to A+ Content Manager in Amazon Seller Central"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Start Creating A+ Content</h3>
          <p>
            Click on the <strong>"Start creating A+ content"</strong> button. You will be prompted to choose between two
            content types:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Basic Enhanced Product Description:</strong> Allows you to add up to 5 custom modules to showcase
              product features.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Brand Story:</strong> Displays above your basic content to showcase your brand origin, values, and
              product catalog for deeper brand connection.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <em>For this guide, we will select the Basic Enhanced Content.</em>
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Name Your Project and Choose Modules</h3>
          <p>
            Follow the on-screen prompts to name your content project and set your language. Click{' '}
            <strong>"Add module"</strong> to pick the layout slots you want to use.
          </p>
          <figure>
            <img
              src="path-to-image-adding-modules.jpg"
              alt="Adding content modules in Amazon A+ Content Manager"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
          <p>
            You can add up to five modules and customize them to fit your brand assets. You can also preview how your
            layout appears on both desktop and mobile devices at any time.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Add Your ASINs</h3>
          <p>
            Add parent or child ASINs (or both) to your project in the <strong>ASIN management</strong> section. Search
            for any ASIN within an ASIN family, select the targeted listings, and apply the content.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Review and Submit for Approval</h3>
          <p>
            Carefully review your project and submit it for Amazon approval. Make sure to review{' '}
            <strong>Amazon’s A+ Content Guidelines</strong> beforehand—policy violations can delay approval, which
            typically takes up to seven days.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Sección 4: Conclusión -->
    <section id="conclusion">
      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        When planning your A+ Content, focus on showcasing your product’s most essential features and proactively
        answering common buyer questions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Avoid cluttering your page with wall-to-wall text or irrelevant details. Your primary goal is to deliver clear
        value—and strategically designed visual content is the best way to achieve high conversions.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
